WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.535
-The last time
you were here, we did --

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.636
This was the last time
I saw you -- we did "Hot Ones."

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.837
-Yes.
-And we actually ate

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.572
the hottest wings in the world.
-Right.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.075
-And I don't know if anyone saw
it, but, I mean, this is --

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.576
It was real.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:13.046
We really ate, like,
the hottest wings.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.881
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.683
-It was -- It was not --
It was not great -- for me.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:20.386
-Well, it was -- it was --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.455
-Like --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.724
-I mean, I was --
I was crying but --

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:26.926
-I was, too.
-No, I know.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.127
But the best part --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.862
-Oh, no.
-The best part

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.165
was going backstage
to check on you after the bit,

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.133
'cause I was like --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.401
-No.
-'Cause I was like, dude.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:37.136
I was freaking out,
'cause my mouth was on fire.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.537
And I'm, like,
eating bread and whatever.

00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:39.739
And I was like,
"Oh, I'll go check on Selena,

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.907
see if she's okay."

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.275
And I walked
into your dressing room.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.677
Do you remember?
-Yes, of course I do, vividly.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.746
-You were throwing up
into a sink.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.148
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.284
-Stop.
-You turn around, I go,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.285
"It's gonna be fine.
It won't be that bad."

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:55.154
And you turned around and your
mascara was all down your face.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.622
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.259
And you had drool -- you had
drool coming out of your mouth.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.028
And you go, "Get -- Get out."
-Yes.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.730
[ Laughter ]
That's the nicer version.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.899
-Yeah, that's the nicer version.
-I was like --

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.900
-"Get out," and that's
the last time I saw you.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.702
So I didn't know --
I'm happy you came back.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.836
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.139
You're a good sport.
You're a good sport.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.574
[ Applause ]

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.742
You got a lot going on.
"Dolittle."

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.177
You have a voice
in that movie, "Dolittle."

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.345
-Yeah.
-It comes out on Friday.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.647
-Yeah.
-And "Rare" is out now.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.616
Finally, it's out.
-I know, it's been --

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.252
-I mean --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.556
-It's been 4 years,
4 1/2 years now,

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.490
before I've released anything,
so...

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.060
-Are you happy it's finally out?
-Yes, I am very happy.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.364
I think I had -- I was holding
my breath for four years,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.033
and then, finally,
I just exhaled.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.436
And now it exists.
-Yeah. Now it's out there.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.637
And everyone's loving it,
by the way.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.506
It's getting --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.674
It's a great album.
-Thank you.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.143
-"Rolling Stone" loves it.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.611
"Billboard" calls you
"Triumphant."

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.746
"Variety" said "'Rare' is one of
the best pop albums

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:56.316
to be released
in recent memory."

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.417
"Time" says,
"'Rare' is a pop gift."

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.053
These are great, killer reviews.
-Wow.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.355
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:05.191
-Well, I love --
"Lose You to Love Me"

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.626
was the first thing you --

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.860
the first song you released
off this album.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.895
-Right.
-And, man, oh, man, that was --

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:11.831
That's a great jam.
And I think everyone liked it,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.999
'cause they were like --
'Cause it's personal.

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:17.636
-Yeah. I mean, I think
there came a point in my life

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:21.641
where there were so many things
being said on my behalf.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.777
And I found myself
protecting people

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.712
that didn't really protect me.

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:29.148
'Cause I didn't want, you know,
to start anything.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.652
And I -- But I had a right
to say my side of this story.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:36.522
And I felt like -- I felt like
that was so liberating,

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:40.226
because it almost felt like
I had let it go, personally,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.727
inside of me,
once it was out.

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:45.231
And that -- I mean, that's
the greatest gift, I think.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.666
-It's tough, right?
To just do that.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.200
I mean, I couldn't imagine
writing a song,

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.602
just putting all your feelings
out there.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.537
-Yeah.
-Not only was it received well,

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:54.874
but, like, it might be -- was it
one of your biggest songs ever?

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.642
-Yeah, it was.
-It is your biggest song ever.

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:58.745
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.679
So it's good to take a risk.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:03.049
It feels good,
you take a risk like that.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.417
-It was --
I was very, very grateful.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:07.019
-Broke all sorts of records.
So...

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:10.790
Anyways, I'm happy
the album's out.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.793
You worked on --
Maybe on that song with

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.095
Finneas -- is that
Billie Eilish's brother?

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.065
-Yeah, actually, he --
We finished up the song

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.034
and gave him the song
to produce it himself.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.503
And he did an amazing job.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.406
He's obviously
extremely talented.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:29.275
-Yeah, we talked to him when
Billie Eilish was on, as well.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.610
And I found out --
I don't know if you know this.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:34.513
But you have something in common
with Billie.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:37.750
You're an inspiration
for the song "Bad Guy."

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.719
But not you.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.387
-Am I the bad guy?
-You're not the bad -- no.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.289
-No, I'm kidding.
-The theme song of

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.858
"Wizards of Waverly Place"...
[ Cheers ]

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.527
...was an inspiration --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:51.263
was an inspiration to her --
to getting the tune.

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.032
-That's --
-Isn't that bizarre?

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.133
-I love you.
-So, I thought maybe

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.634
it'd be fun to play --
-I love Billie.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.503
-...to play a little bit
and see if we can see...

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.271
-Oh, gosh. Okay.
-...what inspired her.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:03.542
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:04.977
-Here's a little bit
of "Wizards."

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.012
-Okay.
-Okay?

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.280
-Oh, no.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.280
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.716
♪♪

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.584
-♪ Well, you know everything
is gonna be a breeze ♪

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.485
♪ That the end will,
no doubt, justify the means ♪

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:15.687
♪ You could fix any problem
with the slightest of ease ♪

00:04:15.687 --> 00:04:16.789
♪ Yes, please ♪

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.158
-Oh, my God!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.826
♪ Ba, ba-doo doo ♪

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.194
-Yeah.
-That's kind of -- right?

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:23.762
Here's "Bad Guy."

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:25.531
[ "Bad Guy" plays ]

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.136
♪♪

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.870
-That's so cool.
-Kinda, right?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.005
Isn't that cool?
-That's so cool.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.173
-That's pretty fun.
I think that's cool.

00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:37.209
What do you want people
to take away from the album

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:38.244
when they listen to it?

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:39.579
'Cause you got
a lot of tracks on here.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.280
-Yeah.
-13.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:45.250
-I think what was most important
for me with this record

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.254
is to make sure
that every single song,

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:50.857
whether it was the lyric
to the production,

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:54.527
to mean something
and to actually hold weight.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.997
And, you know, one of my
favorite songs is "Vulnerable"

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.200
on the track and --
or, "Vulnerable" on the album.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.037
And I think it's --
it was a way of me hoping...

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:07.440
like, hoping I could just
be a voice for people

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.709
who are in
the same situation I'm in,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:13.145
whether it's something mentally
that people struggle with

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.981
or relationships, friendships.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.916
I wanted to be as honest
as I could.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:20.786
And the only thing that I wanted
was to make people feel good.

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:24.190
And, you know, during all
the mess that's happening,

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.493
I think that I'm very lucky
to be in a position

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.128
where I can make people
feel good.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:31.664
-Did you always know the album
was gonna be called "Rare"?

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.065
-Yes.
-You did?

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.735
-The moment we started
four years ago.

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:38.003
-Is that right?
-We worked on "Rare."

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:41.040
And I just said,
before we finished anything,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.108
I said, "This is gonna be
the name of my album."

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:46.045
-Really?
-The word is so special.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.379
And it means a lot.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:50.616
And I think, in this time,
where everyone is obsessed

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:53.586
with feeling like
they need to look the same way

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:56.855
or get things done
or whatever it may be --

00:05:56.855 --> 00:05:59.091
And I mean, I'm --
Obviously, I don't judge.

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.926
I'm just saying there are
some girls who are hurting

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:03.796
because they feel like
they don't fit in.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:07.466
But this word
is eliminating that,

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.701
because you weren't meant
to look like everyone else.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.103
You're meant to be who you are,

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:13.005
and that's unique,
and that's rare.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:16.142
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.410
-Awesome, buddy.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.012
I love every single thing.
-Thanks so much.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.114
-Congrats on the album.
It's out now.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.582
"Dolittle" is out Friday.
Are there --

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.150
Is there any other --
I always feel like --

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.620
'Cause, like, for me,
if I put out a record,

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.456
if there's 13 tracks,
I probably -- that is --

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.124
That's all I wrote was 13.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:33.225
-Maybe 10, you know?

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.627
And I put two bonus things
on there.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.161
-Sure.
-But I feel like a real artist

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:38.063
probably -- do you have, like,
other songs that didn't make it

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:40.066
to "Rare" that are out?
That are done?

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.667
Finished?

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.903
-Maybe there's a few things.
Yeah.

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:49.575
There's a few other songs that I
couldn't help but want to exist.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.076
So I can't really tell when,

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:53.545
but one of my favorite tracks
is called "Boyfriend."

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.848
So I can't wait for people
to hear that one.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.049
-Wow.
That's awesome.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.651
I love you.
It was good to see you.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:00.786
Selena, I love you.
You're the best, buddy.

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:04.524
Selena Gomez, everybody!
"Rare" is out now!

